  "response": "**VERDICT: REVISE**\n\n**Overall Assessment**: The carousel implements basic interactive controls but fails core accessibility design requirements for dynamic content and composite widget patterns. Missing `aria-live` communication, absent active-state indicators, and generic alt text create significant barriers for screen reader users. The component passes a superficial DOM check but breaks the interaction model expected by assistive technology.\n\n**Pre-commitment Predictions** (Phase 1):\nBased on custom carousel/slider patterns, I predicted:\n1. Missing `aria-live` region for dynamic image updates\n2. Indicators lacking active-state communication (`aria-selected`/`aria-current`)\n3. Container missing semantic labeling/context\n4. Generic/dynamic alt text failing descriptive purpose\n5. Incomplete keyboard navigation for indicator group\n*Actual findings align with predictions. All 5 gaps confirmed in code.*\n\n**Critical Findings** (blocks access):\n1. **Dynamic image changes are silent to assistive technology.** \n   - Evidence: `src/BuggyCarousel.jsx:18` (`<img src={images[currentIndex]} alt={`Carousel image ${currentIndex + 1}`} />`) updates visually but has no `aria-live` region or live-region wrapper. State changes only via React re-render.\n   - User group impacted: Screen reader users\n   - WCAG/APG citation: WCAG 4.1.3 Status Messages; WAI-ARIA APG Composite Widget pattern requires dynamic state updates to be announced.\n   - Fix: Wrap the image container in `<div aria-live=\"polite\" aria-atomic=\"true\">` or use a dedicated status region that announces the new image description when `currentIndex` changes.\n\n2. **Indicator buttons do not communicate active state to assistive technology.**\n   - Evidence: `src/BuggyCarousel.jsx:33` (`className={idx === currentIndex ? 'active' : ''}`) relies solely on CSS class for visual state. No `aria-selected=\"true\"` or `aria-current=\"page\"` is present.\n   - User group impacted: Screen reader users, cognitive accessibility users\n   - WCAG/APG citation: WCAG 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value; APG Composite Widget pattern requires active items in indicator groups to expose state programmatically.\n   - Fix: Add `aria-selected={idx === currentIndex}` (or `aria-current=\"page\"`) to each indicator button. Screen readers will announce \"image X, button, selected\".\n\n**Major Findings** (significantly degrades experience):\n1. **Carousel region lacks labeling and semantic structure.**\n   - Evidence: `src/BuggyCarousel.jsx:16` (`<div className=\"carousel\">`) is an unlabeled generic container. No `<figure>`, `<section>`, or `aria-label` provides context.\n   - User group impacted: Screen reader users navigating by landmarks/regions\n   - WCAG/APG citation: WCAG 1.3.1 Info and Relationships; APG recommends labeling custom widget containers for context.\n   - Fix: Replace outer `<div>` with `<figure aria-label=\"Image carousel\">` or add `role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Image carousel\"` to the container.\n\n2. **Alt text is generic and position-dependent rather than descriptive.**\n   - Evidence: `src/BuggyCarousel.jsx:19` (`alt={`Carousel image ${currentIndex + 1}`}`)\n   - User group impacted: Screen reader users, low vision users relying on alt text\n   - WCAG/APG citation: WCAG 1.1.1 Non-text Content; alt text must convey the same information as the visual content. Position-based labels fail this requirement.\n   - Fix: Pass descriptive alt text per image via props (`images.map((img, idx) => <img src={img.src} alt={img.alt || `Slide ${idx + 1}: ${img.description}`}>`)`), or use a static descriptive label if images are purely decorative/illustrative.\n\n3. **Indicator group lacks composite widget keyboard navigation.**\n   - Evidence: `src/BuggyCarousel.jsx:30-35` renders buttons in DOM order with no arrow key, Home, or End handlers.\n   - User group impacted: Keyboard-only users\n   - WCAG/APG citation: WCAG 2.1.1 Keyboard; APG Composite Widget pattern requires arrow keys to navigate indicator groups, Home/End for first/last, and roving tabindex (`tabindex=\"-1\"` on inactive, `0` on active).\n   - Fix: Implement arrow key navigation on the indicators container. Add `role=\"radiogroup\"` or `role=\"listbox\"` to the container, apply roving tabindex, and wire up `ArrowRight`/`ArrowLeft` handlers to update `currentIndex`.\n\n**Minor Findings** (friction but workaround exists):\n- **Focus indicator on indicators may lack sufficient contrast.** If `.active` only changes background color without a visible outline or border change, keyboard focus may be indistinguishable from hover state. Ensure focus ring meets 3:1 contrast against adjacent colors (WCAG 2.4.7).\n- **Button text redundancy.** `aria-label=\"Previous image\"` on `<button>Previous</button>` creates redundant speech (\"Previous image button Previous\"). Fix by removing `aria-label` and relying on visible text, or use `aria-label=\"Previous slide\"` if visual text is purely decorative.\n\n**Enhancements** (best practice not met):\n- **Pause control for auto-play.** If this component gains auto-advance functionality, WCAG 2.2.2 Pause, Stop, Hide requires a visible pause/stop button or user-initiated pause before starting. Not currently in code but critical for carousel patterns.\n- **Skip link to carousel controls.** For pages with multiple carousels, add a visually-hidden skip link targeting the carousel region to reduce tab traversal.\n\n**What's Missing** (gaps, unhandled edge cases, unstated assumptions):\n- Missing `aria-live` region for dynamic content updates\n- Missing active-state ARIA attributes on indicator buttons\n- Missing container labeling/semantic wrapper (`<figure>` or `role=\"region\"`)\n- Missing roving tabindex and arrow key navigation for the indicator group\n- Missing descriptive alt text per image (replaced with generic position labels)\n- Missing pause/stop control infrastructure (if auto-play is added later)\n\n**Multi-Perspective Notes**:\n| Perspective | Alarm Level | Trigger Signal |\n|-------------|-------------|----------------|\n| Screen reader | HIGH | Silent dynamic updates, missing active state, generic alt text |\n| Keyboard-only | MEDIUM | DOM-order tabbing works but lacks arrow key navigation for indicators |\n| Low vision | LOW | Buttons have visible text; focus contrast depends on CSS not provided |\n| Cognitive | MEDIUM | Position-based labels (\"Carousel image 1\") are confusing without context |\n\n**Verdict Justification**: \nThe component implements the visual shell of a carousel but fails the interaction model required by assistive technology. The absence of `aria-live` communication means screen reader users cannot perceive content changes. Missing active-state attributes on indicators breaks position tracking. Generic alt text violates descriptive purpose requirements. These are not preference issues; they are pattern incompleteness per WAI-ARIA APG composite widget guidelines. The code passes basic DOM structure checks but fails real assistive technology interaction. **REVISE** is required before shipping. Upgrading to ACCEPT requires: (1) adding `aria-live` for state changes, (2) implementing `aria-selected`/roving tabindex on indicators, (3) replacing generic alt text with descriptive per-image labels, and (4) labeling the container region.\n\n**Open Questions (unscored)**:\n- Does the parent application provide a global carousel context or framework that auto-handles live regions? (If yes, verify it renders correctly in the DOM.)\n- Are indicator buttons intended to be focusable via roving tabindex, or should they remain in static DOM order per design decision?\n- Will images ever be purely decorative? If so, `alt=\"\"` and `aria-hidden=\"true\"` would be more appropriate than position-based labels.",
